{"name":"Aubergine","hex":"#372528","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aubergine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An Asian plant, Solanum melongena, cultivated for its edible purple, green, or white ovoid fruit; eggplant.","The fruit of this plant, eaten as a vegetable."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aubergine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aubergine (London restaurant)","blocks":[{"text":"Aubergine was a restaurant in Chelsea, London. Owned by A-Z Restaurants, it was opened under chef Gordon Ramsay in 1993. Aubergine was awarded two Michelin stars in 1997, which it held until Ramsay left the restaurant in July 1998 following the firing of Marcus Wareing from sister restaurant L'Oranger. It subsequently reopened and held a single Michelin star under William Drabble until he left the restaurant in 2009. Aubergine closed in 2010, pending a relaunch as an informal Italian restaurant."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aubergine_(London_restaurant)","wikidata":"Q4819030"},{"title":"Aubergine (Netherlands restaurant)","blocks":[{"text":"Aubergine is a restaurant in Steyl in the Netherlands. It is a fine dining restaurant that is awarded one Michelin star in the period 2006–2018."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Restaurant_Aubergine.jpg/330px-Restaurant_Aubergine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aubergine_(Netherlands_restaurant)","wikidata":"Q2469108"},{"title":"Eggplant","blocks":[{"text":"Solanum melongena is a plant species in the nightshade family Solanaceae, grown worldwide for its edible fruit, typically used as a vegetable in cooking. It is known by a number of names, including eggplant, aubergine, and brinjal."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Solanum_melongena_24_08_2012_%281%29.JPG/330px-Solanum_melongena_24_08_2012_%281%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggplant","wikidata":"Q7540"},{"title":"Eggplant (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Eggplant is a dark purple or brownish-purple color that resembles the color of the outer skin of European eggplants. Another name for the color eggplant is aubergine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fb/Aubergine.jpg/330px-Aubergine.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eggplant_(color)","wikidata":"Q1403218"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG/500px-Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG/1280px-Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG/500px-Eggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEggplant_Flower_in_Hong_Kong.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg/500px-%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg/1280px-%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg/500px-%C3%89pines_sous_branches_de_plante_%C3%A0_%C5%93ufs.jpg?utm_source=e